  "facts": {
    "server-cost": [
      {
        "fact": "Battles run in the players' browsers by default (clientCombat on): each browser simulates its own field and reports the result; the server checks results and simulates only the fields no connected human owns (bots, dropped players, missed deadlines).",
        "src": "docs/design/network.md §14 \"Authority per field\"; docs/ARCHITECTURE.md §1"
      },
      {
        "fact": "In client combat the server does not stream battle snapshots or events (b.snap / b.ev) for combat, so a change to battle events or effects costs the server no bandwidth unless SP_COMBAT=server.",
        "src": "docs/design/network.md §14 \"Why\""
      },
      {
        "fact": "Measured: a 4-player match sends about 0.25 MB per round from the server.",
        "src": "docs/DEPLOY.en.md §0 Resource requirements (Network row)"
      },
      {
        "fact": "Measure, do not guess: SP_TRAFFIC_METER=1 on a dev server, npm run traffic-report -- --reset before a test match and npm run traffic-report after it (per message type and room; MB/s and GB/day; --players 300).",
        "src": "changes/README.md \"Server cost\" (the dev traffic meter); tools/traffic-report.mjs header"
      },
      {
        "fact": "A fragment states server cost as MB/s at peak and GB/day per player, per room and for 300 players, typical and worst case, with a Cap line; Server cost: none only when no server, network or bot code changes.",
        "src": "changes/README.md \"Server cost\"; AGENTS.md Hard rules (Server cost)"
      }
    ]
  }
